WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.310
- Welcome back to the Kelly Clarkson Show.

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:04.710
I've had a great time
filling in for Kelly today,

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:07.110
but before we go, I have
one more story to share

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:08.220
from social media.

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:10.075
This is What I'm Liking.

00:00:10.075 --> 00:00:13.560
(upbeat music)
(audience cheers and claps)

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:15.600
- Now, most things that come
out of a vending machine

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.010
are probably not that good for you.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:18.960
You know, it's soda, chips, cookies.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:21.900
But not this vending machine in Chicago.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.970
It dispenses original artwork

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:26.430
along with vintage and nostalgic items.

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:28.080
Everything is $20 or less

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:30.270
and the machine takes credit cards.

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:34.320
The best part, profits go
directly to the artists.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.180
Wonderful.
(audience cheers and claps)

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:38.550
So let's get the creator
of this project in here,

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:42.241
say hi to Steph, watching
on NBC Chicago at three.

00:00:42.241 --> 00:00:44.970
(audience cheers and claps)

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:46.410
- Hi Steph.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:47.400
This is such a cool idea.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.530
So what kind of things can
you buy in this machine?

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:50.760
- So that's a great question.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:54.840
You know, the short answer
is all kinds of things.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:58.080
The main restriction is that
the machine itself is set up

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:01.890
to vend, like you said, a
bag of chips or a candy bar.

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:04.770
So it's about figuring out
how to take the artwork

00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:07.590
that's being made and translate
it to a vendable size.

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:12.590
So we've had stickers,
pins, patches, bird bingo,

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:16.140
this is like all the birds that
you can see around Chicago,

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:18.090
so you can play it as you walk.

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:22.800
We have plant dyed scrunchies,
zines, mystery items.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:25.920
I mean, truly, if you can vend it, I will.

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:28.080
- And where are you setting
up these vending machines?

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:30.990
- So right now there's two live machines

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:33.270
and one in the works that's being painted.

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:35.970
The first one ever was at
the Chicago Cultural Center,

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:38.250
which is like, an amazing
city arts building.

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:41.460
And then the second one, a
great bird-watching location,

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:42.900
is at Metropolitan Brewing.

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:47.900
So each machine is geared towards
the location that it's in.

00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:51.000
So it's like a great
opportunity to collaborate.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.160
It's been super fun,
not just to collaborate

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:57.120
with local artists and
get them an opportunity

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:59.430
to maybe be in front of
audiences that didn't know

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:01.590
that they were ready to be art shopping,

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:04.230
and then also a wider network of people

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:06.390
that are doing weird stuff
with vending machines.

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:07.638
There are a lot of us.

00:02:07.638 --> 00:02:10.830
- (laughs) There are a lot
of people doing weird stuff

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:13.410
with vending machines? That's awesome.

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:16.200
My wife and I met in Chicago,
so when we're back there,

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:17.700
we're gonna check out
your vending machines.

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:18.533
Thank you, Steph.

00:02:18.533 --> 00:02:20.899
I am liking your post right now.

00:02:20.899 --> 00:02:23.490
(audience cheers and claps)

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:24.480
- And that's not all.

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:27.960
Kelly's season long partner,
Pilot pen makers of G2,

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:30.150
the go-to pen of the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:33.750
want to honor truly unstoppable
people just like you, Steph.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:37.448
So they will be writing
you a check for $1,000.

00:02:37.448 --> 00:02:41.212
(audience cheers and claps)

00:02:41.212 --> 00:02:42.958
- Oh my God, thank you.

00:02:42.958 --> 00:02:43.791
- [Host] You deserve it.

00:02:43.791 --> 00:02:46.800
Thank you to all of our
guests today, Marie Bartlett,

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.900
Annaleigh Ashford, Quentin Clare,

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:51.540
Ann Lauren (indistinct), and the dancers.

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:54.630
Kelly will be back tomorrow,
and as she always says,

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:57.513
have a great day, and
if it's not, change it.

